  "interface": {
    "automatic_compiler_inputs": "Finite checked scope, old and new forward declarations, old acceptance certificate. No changed set, unchanged-row proof or custom inverse supplied.",
    "difference_computation": "Compare the two forward functions on every public response of each in-scope row; filter the finite scope by inequality.",
    "minimality_scope": "Minimal among sets whose complement preserves exact row equality. Not minimal for probabilistic game equivalence, reachable responses, actual labels or proof size.",
    "path_generator": "Uses an explicit ordered enumeration of the checked scope, filters changed rows, and creates one replacement per remaining occurrence. Duplicates are allowed generically; MAC rows are proved duplicate-free and cover the exact scope.",
    "path_endpoint": "New declaration inside the enumerated scope, old declaration outside. Compiled equivalences still use identity outside the checked scope.",
    "diagrams": "refl, distinct-row exchange, cons, symm, trans. Concrete exchangeCell is executable; order_cell_exists is a Nonempty theorem from a permutation proposition, not an extracted arbitrary sorting algorithm.",
    "what_is_changed": "Declarations of representation edits at the same actual execution cut. Row replacements are proof-construction operations, not successive native cache writes or new oracle queries.",
    "intermediate_validity": "If old and final declarations are accepted on the enumerated scope, every generated replacement-prefix declaration is accepted too."
  },
